          title: 'Victoria Memorial & Maidan at Dawn',
          text: 'Arrive at the Maidan (the vast central park) at 7am when Kolkata\'s morning rituals unfold: cricket matches on every patch of grass, yoga practitioners, and balloon sellers. Walk to Victoria Memorial (opens 10am, ₹200 foreigners) — the white Makrana marble palace built in 1906 as a monument to Queen Victoria, now a museum housing 25,000 artefacts of British India. The building is one of the most beautiful colonial structures in Asia. The grounds are worth ₹30 even without the museum entry.',
          tip: 'The Victoria Memorial gardens open at sunrise (₹30 entry) before the museum itself opens at 10am — arrive early for photos without crowds. The reflection in the moat at golden hour is extraordinary.',
